/.claude/*
!/.claude/agents
!/.claude/agents/**
!/.claude/settings.json
/node_modules
/tools
/installers
/cypress/downloads
/cypress/videos
/cypress/screenshots
/presentation.md
/.vscode
/results

# Local secrets — never commit. See credentials.example.json for the shape.
# Deliberately UNANCHORED (no leading /), unlike the entries above, so a copy made in a
# subfolder is ignored too. cypress.env.json and .env* are pure safety nets: this repo uses
# neither, but Cypress auto-loads the first and half the tutorials on the internet tell people
# to create the second.
# credentials*.json, not credentials.json: Windows hides file extensions by default, so
# "rename the copy to credentials.json" routinely produces credentials.json.json, and Explorer's
# "credentials - Copy.json" is the other common slip. All of them hold real passwords.
credentials*.json
!credentials.example.json
cypress.env.json
.env
.env.*
